#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""mesh: messaging and lifecycle for Claude Code / agy agents running in herdr.

Every message is written to the recipient's mailbox first, then a one-line
"doorbell" is typed into the recipient's herdr pane. A lost doorbell never
loses the message: it waits in the mailbox until `mesh inbox` reads it.
A Claude recipient's doorbell is written into its cross-session inbox (its
socket) instead, or, for a root that takes only messages from its own
permission mode, handed back for a Claude sender to pass on with SendMessage.

State:      $MESH_HOME      (default ~/.local/state/agent-mesh)
Worktrees:  $MESH_WORKTREES (default ~/.local/share/agent-mesh/worktrees)
Identity:   $MESH_RUN / $MESH_SELF / $MESH_PARENT / $MESH_ROLE, injected by
            `mesh spawn`; the run's root is found through $HERDR_PANE_ID.
"""

